window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b307-fd971b04bab404cf.json"]={sha256:"fd971b04bab404cf6b7d05f8df6a931651126cb1187d6a15476d6c280c1afea1",value:{"id":"b307","title":"山陽新幹線","titleEn":"Sanyo Shinkansen","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以山陽新幹線的跨區域高速運輸為背景，建立連續隧道、橋梁與車站的假想剖面。學徒把列車進洞壓力、受電品質與排水維修放在同一系統邊界，分析短隧道間露天段是否改變乘坐舒適與維修需求。","summaryEn":"Use the Sanyo high-speed corridor as the setting for an invented profile containing successive tunnels, bridges and stations. Place entry pressure, current collection and drainage maintenance inside one system boundary. Investigate how a short open section between tunnels can alter pressure exposure, track behaviour and access requirements without treating a simplified pressure estimate as a tunnel certification calculation.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-highspeed","subcategoryTitle":"高速鐵路系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"High-speed rail systems","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-highspeed","learningTags":["rail","rail-highspeed","rail"],"architectureFamily":"rail-system","architectureNodes":[["路線與土建","Alignment and civil works"],["車輛與接觸","Vehicle and contact"],["牽引供電","Traction supply"],["行車控制","Movement control"],["車站與旅客","Stations and passengers"],["監測與維護","Monitoring and maintenance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,1],[3,4],[4,5],[5,0],[5,3]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-system","labels":["路線與土建","車輛與接觸","牽引供電","行車控制","車站與旅客"],"labelsEn":["Alignment and civil works","Vehicle and contact","Traction supply","Movement control","Stations and passengers"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合原創算例：單元 1 得 travel=7.794118 s；單元 2 得 density=0.7914385 kg/m^3；單元 3 得 displacement_flow=190.8 m^3/s。上述三個結果使用各單元明示的不同邊界，不能任意相加或視為實際工程實測值。以第一單元 length 的擾動測試，結果改為 8.573529 s；學徒需先比較單位、敏感度和假設，再決定是否要細化模型。以山陽新幹線的跨區域高速運輸為背景，建立連續隧道、橋梁與車站的假想剖面。學徒把列車進洞壓力、受電品質與排水維修放在同一系統邊界，分析短隧道間露天段是否改變乘坐舒適與維修需求。 最終交付應保留原始輸入、測點時間戳、誤差範圍與無法由簡化式證明的結論。","textEn":"Integrated original exercise: unit 1 gives travel=7.794118 s; unit 2 gives density=0.7914385 kg/m^3; unit 3 gives displacement_flow=190.8 m^3/s. These three results use different explicit boundaries and must not be added or presented as measurements of the real railway. Perturbing length in the first unit changes its result to 8.573529 s. Compare units, sensitivity and assumptions before deciding which model needs refinement. Use the Sanyo high-speed corridor as the setting for an invented profile containing successive tunnels, bridges and stations. Place entry pressure, current collection and drainage maintenance inside one system boundary. Investigate how a short open section between tunnels can alter pressure exposure, track behaviour and access requirements without treating a simplified pressure estimate as a tunnel certification calculation. The final submission should retain original inputs, measurement timestamps, uncertainty ranges and conclusions that the simplified expressions cannot establish.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b307-v16-s1","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞與高海拔壓力與氣體密度","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel & Altitude pressure and air density","description":"本階段聚焦「隧道壓力波傳遞」與「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" and \"Altitude pressure and air density\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b307-v16-01","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「隧道壓力波傳遞」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。入口緩衝設計影響波形上升率，波到達出口的時間與車身到達時間屬不同問題，須分開建立量測觸發。 波傳時間由傳播距離除以聲速決定，與列車走完整段的時間不同。此式只預測到達時序而不預測波幅；洞口形狀、列車頭型和反射決定的壓力變化須用其他流動模型。 在連續隧道與洞口測點之間比較聲波傳播時間和列車通過時間，另列波幅問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「隧道壓力波傳遞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. Entrance treatments affect the rise of the waveform. Wave arrival and train arrival are different events and require separate measurement triggers. Wave travel time is propagation distance divided by sound speed, not the time for the train to traverse the section. This expression predicts arrival timing, not amplitude. Portal geometry, train-nose shape and reflections require additional flow models to predict pressure changes. Compare acoustic travel time with train-passage time between tunnel and portal sensors, treating wave amplitude as a separate problem. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2650 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.794118 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2650 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.794118 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「隧道壓力波傳遞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tunnel pressure-wave travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-01-k1","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel","text":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。入口緩衝設計影響波形上升率，波到達出口的時間與車身到達時間屬不同問題，須分開建立量測觸發。","textEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. Entrance treatments affect the rise of the waveform.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隧道壓力波傳遞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" is correct?","options":["隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口","列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。","空氣體積流率相同就表示任何海拔的散熱質量流率相同"],"optionsEn":["A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.","A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed.","Equal volumetric airflow guarantees equal cooling mass flow at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b307-v16-02","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：定量估算","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隧道壓力波傳遞」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2650 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.794118 s。敏感度：length 單獨增加百分之十至 2915 m，其餘固定，結果為 8.573529 s。模型邊界：一維線性聲學且音速均勻；不預測波幅、微壓波峰值或反射耗散。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2650 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.794118 s. Sensitivity: length, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2915 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.573529 s. Model boundary: One-dimensional linear acoustics with uniform sound speed; amplitude, micro-pressure-wave peaks and reflection losses are not predicted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2650 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.794118 s。敏感度：length 單獨增加百分之十至 2915 m，其餘固定，結果為 8.573529 s。模型邊界：一維線性聲學且音速均勻；不預測波幅、微壓波峰值或反射耗散。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2650 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.794118 s. Sensitivity: length, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2915 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.573529 s. Model boundary: One-dimensional linear acoustics with uniform sound speed; amplitude, micro-pressure-wave peaks and reflection losses are not predicted.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隧道壓力波傳遞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\", which statement holds?","options":["速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2650 m; sound=340 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2650 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.794118 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2650 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.794118 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b307-v16-03","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隧道壓力波傳遞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較壓力波與列車兩種到達時間，加入一次端部反射畫出事件圖，說明單一延遲量無法判斷出口微壓波是否超標。 再以本單元 length 的對照值重算 travel，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare wave and train arrival times, add one end reflection to the event diagram, and explain why travel time alone cannot establish compliance of portal micro-pressure waves. Also recalculate travel for the alternative length value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。","textEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較壓力波與列車兩種到達時間，加入一次端部反射畫出事件圖，說明單一延遲量無法判斷出口微壓波是否超標。 再以本單元 length 的對照值重算 travel，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare wave and train arrival times, add one end reflection to the event diagram, and explain why travel time alone cannot establish compliance of portal micro-pressure waves. Also recalculate travel for the alternative length value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隧道壓力波傳遞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\"?","options":["在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b307-v16-04","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隧道壓力波傳遞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在連續隧道與洞口測點之間比較聲波傳播時間和列車通過時間，另列波幅問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare acoustic travel time with train-passage time between tunnel and portal sensors, treating wave amplitude as a separate problem.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。","textEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隧道壓力波傳遞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。","空氣體積流率相同就表示任何海拔的散熱質量流率相同"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak.","Equal volumetric airflow guarantees equal cooling mass flow at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b307-v16-05","title":"高海拔壓力與氣體密度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Altitude pressure and air density: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Altitude pressure and air density” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"理想氣體密度由絕對壓力除氣體常數與絕對溫度決定，高海拔低壓會減少同體積空氣所攜帶的質量。這同時影響散熱和氣動力，但車廂供氧與醫療需求不能由密度公式單獨決定。 此理想氣體式以絕對壓力和絕對溫度估算空氣密度，壓力不代表氧氣比例。高原環境的密度可影響氣動和冷卻估算，但人員生理與主動加壓系統需要另外分析。 以隧道內外溫度和絕對壓力估算空氣密度，另列壓力波模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ideal-gas density is absolute pressure divided by gas constant and absolute temperature. Lower pressure at altitude reduces the mass carried in a fixed air volume, affecting cooling and aerodynamic loads. Cabin oxygen provision and medical needs cannot be determined by density alone. This ideal-gas expression estimates air density from absolute pressure and temperature; pressure is not an oxygen fraction. Altitude-dependent density can affect aerodynamic and cooling estimates, while human physiology and active pressurisation require separate analysis. Estimate air density from tunnel and outside temperature and absolute pressure, separately identifying the pressure-wave model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Altitude pressure and air density” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=63600 Pa; Rair=287 J/(kg*K); temperature=280 K；計算：density=pressure/(Rair*temperature)=0.7914385 kg/m^3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=63600 Pa; Rair=287 J/(kg*K); temperature=280 K; calculation: density=pressure/(Rair*temperature)=0.7914385 kg/m^3.","failure":"常見誤解：「空氣體積流率相同就表示任何海拔的散熱質量流率相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal volumetric airflow guarantees equal cooling mass flow at every altitude.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Altitude pressure and air density”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-05-k1","title":"高海拔壓力與氣體密度","titleEn":"Altitude pressure and air density","text":"理想氣體密度由絕對壓力除氣體常數與絕對溫度決定，高海拔低壓會減少同體積空氣所攜帶的質量。這同時影響散熱和氣動力，但車廂供氧與醫療需求不能由密度公式單獨決定。","textEn":"Ideal-gas density is absolute pressure divided by gas constant and absolute temperature. Lower pressure at altitude reduces the mass carried in a fixed air volume, affecting cooling and aerodynamic loads.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：空氣體積流率相同就表示任何海拔的散熱質量流率相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal volumetric airflow guarantees equal cooling mass flow at every altitude. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Altitude pressure and air density\" is correct?","options":["空氣體積流率相同就表示任何海拔的散熱質量流率相同","列車截面乘速度就是所有風井各自收到的相同流量","理想氣體密度由絕對壓力除氣體常數與絕對溫度決定，高海拔低壓會減少同體積空氣所攜帶的質量。"],"optionsEn":["Equal volumetric airflow guarantees equal cooling mass flow at every altitude.","Train frontal area times speed is the identical flow received by every ventilation shaft.","Ideal-gas density is absolute pressure divided by gas constant and absolute temperature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"理想氣體密度由絕對壓力除氣體常數與絕對溫度決定，高海拔低壓會減少同體積空氣所攜帶的質量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ideal-gas density is absolute pressure divided by gas constant and absolute temperature. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b307-v16-06","title":"高海拔壓力與氣體密度：定量估算","titleEn":"Altitude pressure and air density: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Altitude pressure and air density” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=63600 Pa; Rair=287 J/(kg*K); temperature=280 K；計算：density=pressure/(Rair*temperature)=0.7914385 kg/m^3。敏感度：pressure 單獨增加百分之十至 69960 Pa，其餘固定，結果為 0.8705824 kg/m^3。模型邊界：乾空氣理想氣體、均勻壓溫；不計濕度與生理反應。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=63600 Pa; Rair=287 J/(kg*K); temperature=280 K; calculation: density=pressure/(Rair*temperature)=0.7914385 kg/m^3. Sensitivity: pressure, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 69960 Pa, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.8705824 kg/m^3. Model boundary: Dry ideal air at uniform pressure and temperature; humidity and physiological response are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用絕對壓力計與校正溫度計，核對感測器是否誤報表壓，並用已知風量估算質量流率檢查冷卻設計假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use absolute-pressure and calibrated temperature sensors, check that gauge pressure is not mistaken for absolute pressure, and compare mass flow inferred from measured volume flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=63600 Pa; Rair=287 J/(kg*K); temperature=280 K；計算：density=pressure/(Rair*temperature)=0.7914385 kg/m^3。敏感度：pressure 單獨增加百分之十至 69960 Pa，其餘固定，結果為 0.8705824 kg/m^3。模型邊界：乾空氣理想氣體、均勻壓溫；不計濕度與生理反應。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=63600 Pa; Rair=287 J/(kg*K); temperature=280 K; calculation: density=pressure/(Rair*temperature)=0.7914385 kg/m^3. Sensitivity: pressure, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 69960 Pa, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.8705824 kg/m^3. Model boundary: Dry ideal air at uniform pressure and temperature; humidity and physiological response are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Altitude pressure and air density\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=63600 Pa; Rair=287 J/(kg*K); temperature=280 K。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=63600 Pa; Rair=287 J/(kg*K); temperature=280 K；計算：density=pressure/(Rair*temperature)=0.7914385 kg/m^3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=63600 Pa; Rair=287 J/(kg*K); temperature=280 K; calculation: density=pressure/(Rair*temperature)=0.7914385 kg/m^3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b307-v16-07","title":"高海拔壓力與氣體密度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Altitude pressure and air density: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Altitude pressure and air density” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用絕對壓力計與校正溫度計，核對感測器是否誤報表壓，並用已知風量估算質量流率檢查冷卻設計假設。 校正絕對壓力計並量測同位置氣溫，核對溫標換算，必要時另列濕度造成的氣體性質差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use absolute-pressure and calibrated temperature sensors, check that gauge pressure is not mistaken for absolute pressure, and compare mass flow inferred from measured volume flow. Calibrate the absolute-pressure sensor and measure temperature at the same location, checking the temperature conversion and separately considering humidity effects. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較兩種絕對壓力下的密度與同風量質量流率，標註溫標換算，再說明哪些車廂環境議題需要其他專業模型。 再以本單元 pressure 的對照值重算 density，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare density and mass flow at two absolute pressures, show temperature-scale conversion, and identify cabin-environment questions requiring additional specialised models. Also recalculate density for the alternative pressure value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：把攝氏溫度直接代入氣體公式會產生巨大誤差；低密度時沿用海平面風量又可能不足以移除同一熱負載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using Celsius directly in the gas equation creates a large error; at low density, sea-level volume flow may not remove the same heat load. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用絕對壓力計與校正溫度計，核對感測器是否誤報表壓，並用已知風量估算質量流率檢查冷卻設計假設。 校正絕對壓力計並量測同位置氣溫，核對溫標換算，必要時另列濕度造成的氣體性質差異。","textEn":"Use absolute-pressure and calibrated temperature sensors, check that gauge pressure is not mistaken for absolute pressure, and compare mass flow inferred from measured volume flow. Calibrate the absolute-pressure sensor and measure temperature at the same location, checking the temperature conversion and separately considering humidity effects.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較兩種絕對壓力下的密度與同風量質量流率，標註溫標換算，再說明哪些車廂環境議題需要其他專業模型。 再以本單元 pressure 的對照值重算 density，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare density and mass flow at two absolute pressures, show temperature-scale conversion, and identify cabin-environment questions requiring additional specialised models. Also recalculate density for the alternative pressure value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Altitude pressure and air density\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","使用絕對壓力計與校正溫度計，核對感測器是否誤報表壓，並用已知風量估算質量流率檢查冷卻設計假設。","只要靜態接觸線高度正確就能保證高速受流品質"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use absolute-pressure and calibrated temperature sensors, check that gauge pressure is not mistaken for absolute pressure, and compare mass flow inferred from measured volume flow.","Correct static contact-wire height alone guarantees good current collection at high speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用絕對壓力計與校正溫度計，核對感測器是否誤報表壓，並用已知風量估算質量流率檢查冷卻設計假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use absolute-pressure and calibrated temperature sensors, check that gauge pressure is not mistaken for absolute pressure, and compare mass flow inferred from measured volume flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b307-v16-08","title":"高海拔壓力與氣體密度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Altitude pressure and air density: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Altitude pressure and air density” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把攝氏溫度直接代入氣體公式會產生巨大誤差；低密度時沿用海平面風量又可能不足以移除同一熱負載。 若使用攝氏溫度直接作分母，空氣密度會失去正確物理意義。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using Celsius directly in the gas equation creates a large error; at low density, sea-level volume flow may not remove the same heat load. Using Celsius temperature directly in the denominator produces a physically incorrect air density. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以隧道內外溫度和絕對壓力估算空氣密度，另列壓力波模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Estimate air density from tunnel and outside temperature and absolute pressure, separately identifying the pressure-wave model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「空氣體積流率相同就表示任何海拔的散熱質量流率相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal volumetric airflow guarantees equal cooling mass flow at every altitude.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把攝氏溫度直接代入氣體公式會產生巨大誤差；低密度時沿用海平面風量又可能不足以移除同一熱負載。 若使用攝氏溫度直接作分母，空氣密度會失去正確物理意義。","textEn":"Using Celsius directly in the gas equation creates a large error; at low density, sea-level volume flow may not remove the same heat load. Using Celsius temperature directly in the denominator produces a physically incorrect air density.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高海拔壓力與氣體密度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Altitude pressure and air density\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","列車截面乘速度就是所有風井各自收到的相同流量","把攝氏溫度直接代入氣體公式會產生巨大誤差；低密度時沿用海平面風量又可能不足以移除同一熱負載。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Train frontal area times speed is the identical flow received by every ventilation shaft.","Using Celsius directly in the gas equation creates a large error; at low density, sea-level volume flow may not remove the same heat load."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把攝氏溫度直接代入氣體公式會產生巨大誤差；低密度時沿用海平面風量又可能不足以移除同一熱負載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using Celsius directly in the gas equation creates a large error; at low density, sea-level volume flow may not remove the same heat load. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b307-v16-s2","title":"列車活塞流量與堵塞比與延遲與制動距離","titleEn":"Train piston flow and blockage ratio & Delay and braking distance","description":"本階段聚焦「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」與「延遲與制動距離」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Train piston flow and blockage ratio\" and \"Delay and braking distance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b307-v16-09","title":"列車活塞流量與堵塞比：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train piston flow and blockage ratio: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Train piston flow and blockage ratio” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車進入受限斷面時排擠空氣，列車截面乘速度提供幾何排量的量級。實際空氣可經車旁間隙、通風井和相鄰隧道分流，因此幾何排量不是某一通風井的實測流量。 列車排開體積的模型首先遵守連續方程，但洩漏、車站開口與可壓縮效應會改變實際流場。應明確使用剩餘通流面積，不能用整個隧道面積忽略車體阻塞。 在隧道橫斷面中分開列車阻塞面積與剩餘通風面積。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A train displaces air in a confined section, and frontal area times speed gives the geometric displacement scale. Air divides through the annular gap, shafts and adjoining tunnels. Geometric displacement therefore does not equal measured flow through a particular ventilation shaft. A displaced-volume model first follows continuity, but leakage, station openings and compressibility alter the actual field. Use the remaining flow area explicitly rather than the whole tunnel area while ignoring train blockage. Separate train blockage area from the remaining ventilation area in a tunnel cross-section. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Train piston flow and blockage ratio” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：train_area=9.54 m^2; speed=20 m/s；計算：displacement_flow=train_area*speed=190.8 m^3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: train_area=9.54 m^2; speed=20 m/s; calculation: displacement_flow=train_area*speed=190.8 m^3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「列車截面乘速度就是所有風井各自收到的相同流量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Train frontal area times speed is the identical flow received by every ventilation shaft.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Train piston flow and blockage ratio”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-09-k1","title":"列車活塞流量與堵塞比","titleEn":"Train piston flow and blockage ratio","text":"列車進入受限斷面時排擠空氣，列車截面乘速度提供幾何排量的量級。實際空氣可經車旁間隙、通風井和相鄰隧道分流，因此幾何排量不是某一通風井的實測流量。","textEn":"A train displaces air in a confined section, and frontal area times speed gives the geometric displacement scale. Air divides through the annular gap, shafts and adjoining tunnels.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：列車截面乘速度就是所有風井各自收到的相同流量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Train frontal area times speed is the identical flow received by every ventilation shaft. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train piston flow and blockage ratio\" is correct?","options":["列車進入受限斷面時排擠空氣，列車截面乘速度提供幾何排量的量級。","列車截面乘速度就是所有風井各自收到的相同流量","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["A train displaces air in a confined section, and frontal area times speed gives the geometric displacement scale.","Train frontal area times speed is the identical flow received by every ventilation shaft.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"列車進入受限斷面時排擠空氣，列車截面乘速度提供幾何排量的量級。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A train displaces air in a confined section, and frontal area times speed gives the geometric displacement scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b307-v16-10","title":"列車活塞流量與堵塞比：定量估算","titleEn":"Train piston flow and blockage ratio: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Train piston flow and blockage ratio” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：train_area=9.54 m^2; speed=20 m/s；計算：displacement_flow=train_area*speed=190.8 m^3/s。敏感度：train_area 單獨增加百分之十至 10.494 m^2，其餘固定，結果為 209.88 m^3/s。模型邊界：不可壓縮幾何排量；未求壓差、流路分配與空氣壓縮。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: train_area=9.54 m^2; speed=20 m/s; calculation: displacement_flow=train_area*speed=190.8 m^3/s. Sensitivity: train_area, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 10.494 m^2, with all other inputs fixed, gives 209.88 m^3/s. Model boundary: Incompressible geometric displacement; pressure difference, path splitting and compressibility are not solved. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以列車位置同步觸發各風井和月台風速量測，檢查流量方向與時間差，避免把瞬時尖峰當成持續換氣能力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trigger shaft and platform air-velocity measurements from train position, inspect direction and delay, and avoid treating a brief peak as continuous ventilation capacity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：train_area=9.54 m^2; speed=20 m/s；計算：displacement_flow=train_area*speed=190.8 m^3/s。敏感度：train_area 單獨增加百分之十至 10.494 m^2，其餘固定，結果為 209.88 m^3/s。模型邊界：不可壓縮幾何排量；未求壓差、流路分配與空氣壓縮。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: train_area=9.54 m^2; speed=20 m/s; calculation: displacement_flow=train_area*speed=190.8 m^3/s. Sensitivity: train_area, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 10.494 m^2, with all other inputs fixed, gives 209.88 m^3/s. Model boundary: Incompressible geometric displacement; pressure difference, path splitting and compressibility are not solved.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train piston flow and blockage ratio\", which statement holds?","options":["橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：train_area=9.54 m^2; speed=20 m/s。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：train_area=9.54 m^2; speed=20 m/s；計算：displacement_flow=train_area*speed=190.8 m^3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: train_area=9.54 m^2; speed=20 m/s; calculation: displacement_flow=train_area*speed=190.8 m^3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b307-v16-11","title":"列車活塞流量與堵塞比：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train piston flow and blockage ratio: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Train piston flow and blockage ratio” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以列車位置同步觸發各風井和月台風速量測，檢查流量方向與時間差，避免把瞬時尖峰當成持續換氣能力。 在列車通過前後同步量測風速、壓力及位置，以多點截面平均避免局部噴流誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trigger shaft and platform air-velocity measurements from train position, inspect direction and delay, and avoid treating a brief peak as continuous ventilation capacity. Synchronise airflow, pressure and train position around passage, using a multipoint section average to avoid bias from local jets. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將總排量分配到兩條假想阻力路徑，畫出質量守恆圖，再說明需要哪些壓差資料才能求分流比例。 再以本單元 train_area 的對照值重算 displacement_flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Divide the displacement among two hypothetical resistance paths, draw the mass balance, and identify the pressure measurements required to determine the split. Also recalculate displacement_flow for the alternative train_area value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：風井受阻時氣流可能轉移到月台，造成局部強風；單一風速計又可能量到回流區而低估主流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A blocked shaft can redirect flow toward the platform and create local gusts; one anemometer inside a recirculation region may underestimate the main flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以列車位置同步觸發各風井和月台風速量測，檢查流量方向與時間差，避免把瞬時尖峰當成持續換氣能力。 在列車通過前後同步量測風速、壓力及位置，以多點截面平均避免局部噴流誤差。","textEn":"Trigger shaft and platform air-velocity measurements from train position, inspect direction and delay, and avoid treating a brief peak as continuous ventilation capacity. Synchronise airflow, pressure and train position around passage, using a multipoint section average to avoid bias from local jets.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將總排量分配到兩條假想阻力路徑，畫出質量守恆圖，再說明需要哪些壓差資料才能求分流比例。 再以本單元 train_area 的對照值重算 displacement_flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Divide the displacement among two hypothetical resistance paths, draw the mass balance, and identify the pressure measurements required to determine the split. Also recalculate displacement_flow for the alternative train_area value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train piston flow and blockage ratio\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點","以列車位置同步觸發各風井和月台風速量測，檢查流量方向與時間差，避免把瞬時尖峰當成持續換氣能力。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.","Trigger shaft and platform air-velocity measurements from train position, inspect direction and delay, and avoid treating a brief peak as continuous ventilation capacity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以列車位置同步觸發各風井和月台風速量測，檢查流量方向與時間差，避免把瞬時尖峰當成持續換氣能力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trigger shaft and platform air-velocity measurements from train position, inspect direction and delay, and avoid treating a brief peak as continuous ventilation capacity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b307-v16-12","title":"列車活塞流量與堵塞比：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train piston flow and blockage ratio: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Train piston flow and blockage ratio” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"風井受阻時氣流可能轉移到月台，造成局部強風；單一風速計又可能量到回流區而低估主流。 局部風速尖峰不能當作整段平均流量，須核對截面分布。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A blocked shaft can redirect flow toward the platform and create local gusts; one anemometer inside a recirculation region may underestimate the main flow. A local velocity peak cannot represent whole-section flow; inspect the cross-sectional distribution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在隧道橫斷面中分開列車阻塞面積與剩餘通風面積。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Separate train blockage area from the remaining ventilation area in a tunnel cross-section.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「列車截面乘速度就是所有風井各自收到的相同流量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Train frontal area times speed is the identical flow received by every ventilation shaft.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"風井受阻時氣流可能轉移到月台，造成局部強風；單一風速計又可能量到回流區而低估主流。 局部風速尖峰不能當作整段平均流量，須核對截面分布。","textEn":"A blocked shaft can redirect flow toward the platform and create local gusts; one anemometer inside a recirculation region may underestimate the main flow. A local velocity peak cannot represent whole-section flow; inspect the cross-sectional distribution.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車活塞流量與堵塞比」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train piston flow and blockage ratio\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["風井受阻時氣流可能轉移到月台，造成局部強風；單一風速計又可能量到回流區而低估主流。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["A blocked shaft can redirect flow toward the platform and create local gusts; one anemometer inside a recirculation region may underestimate the main flow.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"風井受阻時氣流可能轉移到月台，造成局部強風；單一風速計又可能量到回流區而低估主流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A blocked shaft can redirect flow toward the platform and create local gusts; one anemometer inside a recirculation region may underestimate the main flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b307-v16-13","title":"延遲與制動距離：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「延遲與制動距離」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Delay and braking distance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。速度平方項說明高速時少量速度誤差會被放大，固定減速度只能作第一輪界限估算。 延遲項與速度成正比，減速項與速度平方成正比；把兩項分開後，才能選擇改善控制延遲或增加有效制動的方案。若存在坡度，應另加沿坡重力，不能只改總距離。 把隧道內制動後的位置與避難通道的里程分開標示。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「延遲與制動距離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds. Only the deceleration phase removes kinetic energy, so stopping distance includes both a delay term and a braking term. The squared speed dependence amplifies speed uncertainty; constant deceleration is only an initial bounding approximation. The delay term is linear in speed and the deceleration term is quadratic. Separating them reveals whether control latency or effective braking deserves attention. A gradient requires an added gravitational component, not an arbitrary adjustment to the final distance. Mark the post-braking position and emergency-passage chainage separately inside a tunnel. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Delay and braking distance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=74.2 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=4118.1 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=74.2 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=4118.1 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「延遲與制動距離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Delay and braking distance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-13-k1","title":"延遲與制動距離","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance","text":"列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。速度平方項說明高速時少量速度誤差會被放大，固定減速度只能作第一輪界限估算。","textEn":"A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds. Only the deceleration phase removes kinetic energy, so stopping distance includes both a delay term and a braking term.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「延遲與制動距離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Delay and braking distance\" is correct?","options":["速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度"],"optionsEn":["A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b307-v16-14","title":"延遲與制動距離：定量估算","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「延遲與制動距離」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Delay and braking distance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=74.2 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=4118.1 m。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 81.62 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 4962.496 m。模型邊界：水平直線、定減速、無風；沒有建立黏著分布與煞車熱衰退。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=74.2 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=4118.1 m. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 81.62 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 4962.496 m. Model boundary: Level straight track and constant deceleration; adhesion variation and thermal fade are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=74.2 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=4118.1 m。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 81.62 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 4962.496 m。模型邊界：水平直線、定減速、無風；沒有建立黏著分布與煞車熱衰退。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=74.2 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=4118.1 m. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 81.62 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 4962.496 m. Model boundary: Level straight track and constant deceleration; adhesion variation and thermal fade are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「延遲與制動距離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Delay and braking distance\", which statement holds?","options":["兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","只要靜態接觸線高度正確就能保證高速受流品質","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=74.2 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2。"],"optionsEn":["Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","Correct static contact-wire height alone guarantees good current collection at high speed.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=74.2 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=4118.1 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=74.2 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=4118.1 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b307-v16-15","title":"延遲與制動距離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「延遲與制動距離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Delay and braking distance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。 用獨立里程或地速核對輪速積分，報告濕乾軌差異及停車距離的重複試驗範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps. Identify command delay separately from steady deceleration and cross-check distance by integrating measured speed. Check integrated wheel speed against independent distance or ground speed, and report wet-dry differences and repeated stopping-distance ranges. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別增加延遲與初速，畫出兩條停車曲線；寫出哪個區段對各參數敏感，以及需要哪些現場資料才可建立保護曲線。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase delay and initial speed separately, plot both stopping curves, identify the sensitive phase, and list the field evidence needed before defining a protection curve. Also recalculate distance for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。 用獨立里程或地速核對輪速積分，報告濕乾軌差異及停車距離的重複試驗範圍。","textEn":"Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps. Identify command delay separately from steady deceleration and cross-check distance by integrating measured speed. Check integrated wheel speed against independent distance or ground speed, and report wet-dry differences and repeated stopping-distance ranges.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別增加延遲與初速，畫出兩條停車曲線；寫出哪個區段對各參數敏感，以及需要哪些現場資料才可建立保護曲線。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase delay and initial speed separately, plot both stopping curves, identify the sensitive phase, and list the field evidence needed before defining a protection curve. Also recalculate distance for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「延遲與制動距離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Delay and braking distance\"?","options":["對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b307-v16-16","title":"延遲與制動距離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「延遲與制動距離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Delay and braking distance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 應比較壓力建立與地速下降先後，避免誤判煞車故障。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. Compare pressure build-up with ground-speed decay before diagnosing a brake fault. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把隧道內制動後的位置與避難通道的里程分開標示。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mark the post-braking position and emergency-passage chainage separately inside a tunnel.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 應比較壓力建立與地速下降先後，避免誤判煞車故障。","textEn":"Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. Compare pressure build-up with ground-speed decay before diagnosing a brake fault.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「延遲與制動距離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Delay and braking distance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b307-v16-s3","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度與橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration & Bridge deflection and span sensitivity","description":"本階段聚焦「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」與「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\" and \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b307-v16-17","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。超高平衡速度只對特定半徑和速度成立，慢車可能出現超高過剩；不能把增加超高當成所有車種都受益的措施。 殘餘加速度的正負表示側向作用方向，而不是安全與危險的二元判斷。半徑、軌距與高差必須使用一致長度單位，車體感受還會受到懸吊轉角影響。 比較洞口附近曲線的平衡速度與低速維修列車工況。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration. Equilibrium cant applies to one radius and speed. A slower service can experience cant excess, so increasing cant does not improve every train condition. The sign of residual acceleration identifies its lateral direction, not a binary safe-unsafe outcome. Radius, gauge and rail-level difference require consistent length units. Carbody response is additionally affected by suspension rotation, which this geometric estimate does not resolve. Compare curve equilibrium speed near a portal with a slow maintenance-train condition. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.22644 m/s^2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=63.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.22644 m/s^2.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cant and unbalanced acceleration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-17-k1","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration","text":"曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。超高平衡速度只對特定半徑和速度成立，慢車可能出現超高過剩；不能把增加超高當成所有車種都受益的措施。","textEn":"On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration. Equilibrium cant applies to one radius and speed.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\" is correct?","options":["任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"曲線需求的向心加速度由重力沿軌道平面的分量與輪軌側向作用共同提供。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"On a curve, the component of gravity in the track plane and wheel-rail lateral forces together provide centripetal acceleration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b307-v16-18","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：定量估算","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.22644 m/s^2。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 69.96 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.4388004 m/s^2。模型邊界：小角度近似與剛性車體；未計懸吊側滾、動態輪重減載和規範允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=63.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.22644 m/s^2. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 69.96 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.4388004 m/s^2. Model boundary: Small-angle approximation and rigid body; suspension roll, dynamic wheel unloading and acceptance limits are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.22644 m/s^2。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 69.96 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.4388004 m/s^2。模型邊界：小角度近似與剛性車體；未計懸吊側滾、動態輪重減載和規範允收值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=63.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.22644 m/s^2. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 69.96 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.4388004 m/s^2. Model boundary: Small-angle approximation and rigid body; suspension roll, dynamic wheel unloading and acceptance limits are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=63.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m；計算：residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.22644 m/s^2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=63.6 m/s; R=4000 m; gauge=1.5 m; cant=0.12 m; calculation: residual=v*v/R-9.81*cant/gauge=0.22644 m/s^2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b307-v16-19","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。 用實測半徑和高差重算平衡速度，保留感測器安裝角的校正值及量測不確定度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings. Recalculate equilibrium speed from measured radius and cant, retaining mounting-angle corrections and uncertainty for the acceleration sensor. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：選兩種速度共同計算殘餘加速度，找出符號反轉位置，說明為何混合服務需要速度分布而非單一最高速度。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 residual，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate residual acceleration for two speeds, locate its sign reversal, and explain why mixed services require a speed distribution rather than one maximum speed. Also recalculate residual for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。 用實測半徑和高差重算平衡速度，保留感測器安裝角的校正值及量測不確定度。","textEn":"Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings. Recalculate equilibrium speed from measured radius and cant, retaining mounting-angle corrections and uncertainty for the acceleration sensor.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"選兩種速度共同計算殘餘加速度，找出符號反轉位置，說明為何混合服務需要速度分布而非單一最高速度。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 residual，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Calculate residual acceleration for two speeds, locate its sign reversal, and explain why mixed services require a speed distribution rather than one maximum speed. Also recalculate residual for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。","空氣體積流率相同就表示任何海拔的散熱質量流率相同"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings.","Equal volumetric airflow guarantees equal cooling mass flow at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在相同半徑區段量測軌面高差與橫向加速度，扣除感測器安裝角度，並把車體讀值與軌道平面讀值分開記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure rail level difference and lateral acceleration on the same curve, remove sensor mounting angle, and distinguish carbody readings from track-plane readings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b307-v16-20","title":"曲線超高與未平衡加速度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cant and unbalanced acceleration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cant and unbalanced acceleration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 需核對高差符號與曲線方向，防止左右軌互換。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. Check cant sign against curve direction to prevent swapping the inner and outer rails. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較洞口附近曲線的平衡速度與低速維修列車工況。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare curve equilibrium speed near a portal with a slow maintenance-train condition.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 需核對高差符號與曲線方向，防止左右軌互換。","textEn":"Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. Check cant sign against curve direction to prevent swapping the inner and outer rails.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「曲線超高與未平衡加速度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cant and unbalanced acceleration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只依高速通過最佳化超高，可能讓慢車或停車承受反向側向力；感測器橫滾又會把重力投影混入振動訊號。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Cant optimised only for fast trains can impose reverse lateral loading on slow or stopped trains; sensor roll also mixes gravity into vibration measurements. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b307-v16-21","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。鐵道橋還需要動態與軌道相互作用檢查，靜態梁算例只用來辨認參數量級。 跨長四次方使幾何誤差特別重要，但只有在相同支承、均布荷載及截面條件下才可比較。將毫米轉成公尺後再核對剛度，可避免把量測位移誤差變成材料性能判斷。 檢查短橋跨的靜態撓度並指出移動列車動力仍待分析。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. Section inertia and material stiffness jointly resist bending. A railway bridge also requires dynamic and track-interaction checks; this static beam exercise only reveals parameter magnitudes. Fourth-power span dependence makes geometry important, but comparison requires the same support, uniform-load and section assumptions. Convert millimetres and metres consistently before checking stiffness, so a displacement-unit error does not become a false conclusion about material properties. Check static deflection of a short bridge and identify the remaining moving-train dynamic analysis. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.5 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.146659 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.5 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.146659 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-21-k1","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity","text":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。鐵道橋還需要動態與軌道相互作用檢查，靜態梁算例只用來辨認參數量級。","textEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. Section inertia and material stiffness jointly resist bending.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" is correct?","options":["簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":0,"explanation":"簡支梁在均布荷載下的撓度對跨長有四次方敏感度，截面慣性矩與材料剛度共同抵抗彎曲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For a simply supported beam under uniform load, deflection scales with the fourth power of span. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b307-v16-22","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：定量估算","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.5 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.146659 mm。敏感度：L 單獨增加百分之十至 29.15 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.678823 mm。模型邊界：簡支Euler梁、小撓度、靜態均布荷載；不代表列車移動荷載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.5 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.146659 mm. Sensitivity: L, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 29.15 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.678823 mm. Model boundary: Simply supported Euler beam, small deflection and static uniform load; not a moving train-load analysis. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.5 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.146659 mm。敏感度：L 單獨增加百分之十至 29.15 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.678823 mm。模型邊界：簡支Euler梁、小撓度、靜態均布荷載；不代表列車移動荷載。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.5 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.146659 mm. Sensitivity: L, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 29.15 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.678823 mm. Model boundary: Simply supported Euler beam, small deflection and static uniform load; not a moving train-load analysis.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\", which statement holds?","options":["只要靜態接觸線高度正確就能保證高速受流品質","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.5 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Correct static contact-wire height alone guarantees good current collection at high speed.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：w=50000 N/m; L=26.5 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4；計算：deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.146659 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: w=50000 N/m; L=26.5 m; E=3.5e+10 Pa; I=8 m^4; calculation: deflection=5*w*L**4/(384*E*I)*1000=1.146659 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b307-v16-23","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 先以已知荷載校對位移計量程與零點，分別記錄載入卸載路徑及支點運動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Check displacement-sensor range and zero under known loading, recording loading and unloading paths separately from support movement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持截面不變增加跨長，再比較提高慣性矩的補償幅度，說明靜態位移符合預期為何仍不能取代動態驗證。 再以本單元 L 的對照值重算 deflection，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase span while keeping the section fixed, calculate the compensating inertia change, and explain why agreement in static deflection cannot replace dynamic verification. Also recalculate deflection for the alternative L value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 先以已知荷載校對位移計量程與零點，分別記錄載入卸載路徑及支點運動。","textEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Check displacement-sensor range and zero under known loading, recording loading and unloading paths separately from support movement.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持截面不變增加跨長，再比較提高慣性矩的補償幅度，說明靜態位移符合預期為何仍不能取代動態驗證。 再以本單元 L 的對照值重算 deflection，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase span while keeping the section fixed, calculate the compensating inertia change, and explain why agreement in static deflection cannot replace dynamic verification. Also recalculate deflection for the alternative L value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","列車截面乘速度就是所有風井各自收到的相同流量","在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Train frontal area times speed is the identical flow received by every ventilation shaft.","Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在已知載重位置量測跨中和支點位移，扣除支承沉陷後對照彎矩圖，並用卸載後讀值檢查是否存在殘留變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure midspan and support movement under known loading, subtract support settlement, compare with the moment diagram, and inspect residual displacement after unloading. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b307-v16-24","title":"橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bridge deflection and span sensitivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 若卸載後仍有位移，須區分基座滑移與構件殘留變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Residual displacement after unloading requires distinguishing fixture slip from permanent structural deformation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查短橋跨的靜態撓度並指出移動列車動力仍待分析。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Check static deflection of a short bridge and identify the remaining moving-train dynamic analysis.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 若卸載後仍有位移，須區分基座滑移與構件殘留變形。","textEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Residual displacement after unloading requires distinguishing fixture slip from permanent structural deformation.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橋梁撓度與跨長敏感度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bridge deflection and span sensitivity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":0,"explanation":"支承鬆動或局部開裂可能改變有效剛度，若把所有位移都當成梁彎曲，校準出的彈性模數就會失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loose supports and local cracking alter effective stiffness; interpreting all displacement as beam bending produces a misleading calibrated elastic modulus. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b307-v16-s4","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折與集水與排水容量","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink & Catchment inflow and drainage capacity","description":"本階段聚焦「沉陷差與軌道坡折」與「集水與排水容量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Differential settlement and track kink\" and \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b307-v16-25","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「沉陷差與軌道坡折」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential settlement and track kink” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。兩端高差除以基長只給平均坡度，無法描述局部尖峰；需要多點剖面才能辨認曲率與變形長度。 相同端點坡度可以對應完全不同的中間形狀，因此坡度不能單獨表示軌道曲率。測點間距必須小於欲辨認的變形尺度，並將高程誤差相對於基長傳遞到坡度結果。 在路堤、橋台與隧道銜接處設計多點高程剖面。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉陷差與軌道坡折」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. End-to-end difference divided by baseline gives only an average gradient, not a local peak. A spatial profile is needed to identify curvature and deformation length. Identical endpoint gradient can hide very different intermediate shapes, so gradient alone cannot describe track curvature. Survey spacing must resolve the deformation length scale, and elevation uncertainty must be propagated relative to the baseline into the reported gradient. Design multipoint elevation profiles across embankment, abutment and tunnel transitions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential settlement and track kink” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01272 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.636 mm/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.01272 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.636 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential settlement and track kink”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-25-k1","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink","text":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。兩端高差除以基長只給平均坡度，無法描述局部尖峰；需要多點剖面才能辨認曲率與變形長度。","textEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. End-to-end difference divided by baseline gives only an average gradient, not a local peak.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉陷差與軌道坡折」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Differential settlement and track kink\" is correct?","options":["兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b307-v16-26","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：定量估算","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential settlement and track kink” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01272 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.636 mm/m。敏感度：drop 單獨增加百分之十至 0.013992 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.6996 mm/m。模型邊界：小變形平均坡度；不計車軌耦合動力或容許軌道幾何。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.01272 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.636 mm/m. Sensitivity: drop, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.013992 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.6996 mm/m. Model boundary: Small-deformation average gradient; vehicle-track dynamics and permissible geometry limits are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01272 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.636 mm/m。敏感度：drop 單獨增加百分之十至 0.013992 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.6996 mm/m。模型邊界：小變形平均坡度；不計車軌耦合動力或容許軌道幾何。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.01272 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.636 mm/m. Sensitivity: drop, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.013992 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.6996 mm/m. Model boundary: Small-deformation average gradient; vehicle-track dynamics and permissible geometry limits are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Differential settlement and track kink\", which statement holds?","options":["煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點","空氣體積流率相同就表示任何海拔的散熱質量流率相同","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01272 m; baseline=20 m。"],"optionsEn":["A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.","Equal volumetric airflow guarantees equal cooling mass flow at every altitude.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01272 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.636 mm/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.01272 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.636 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b307-v16-27","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉陷差與軌道坡折」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential settlement and track kink” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 重複觀測同一測點並做閉合檢核，以另一穩定基準核對零點，報告高差與基長各自誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Repeat identical points with closure checks, verify zero against another stable reference, and report separate errors for elevation difference and baseline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：構造端點相同但中間下陷的剖面，與直線坡度模型比較；提出足以辨識沉陷槽寬度的測點間距與複測頻率。 再以本單元 drop 的對照值重算 gradient，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Construct a profile with equal endpoints and an intermediate trough, compare it with a straight-gradient model, and propose spacing and repeat intervals able to resolve the trough. Also recalculate gradient for the alternative drop value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 重複觀測同一測點並做閉合檢核，以另一穩定基準核對零點，報告高差與基長各自誤差。","textEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Repeat identical points with closure checks, verify zero against another stable reference, and report separate errors for elevation difference and baseline.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"構造端點相同但中間下陷的剖面，與直線坡度模型比較；提出足以辨識沉陷槽寬度的測點間距與複測頻率。 再以本單元 drop 的對照值重算 gradient，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Construct a profile with equal endpoints and an intermediate trough, compare it with a straight-gradient model, and propose spacing and repeat intervals able to resolve the trough. Also recalculate gradient for the alternative drop value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉陷差與軌道坡折」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Differential settlement and track kink\"?","options":["採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b307-v16-28","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：失效診斷","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential settlement and track kink” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 高差異常需先查基點，不能立刻推定路基局部下沉。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. An unusual level difference requires a datum check before inferring local earthwork settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在路堤、橋台與隧道銜接處設計多點高程剖面。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Design multipoint elevation profiles across embankment, abutment and tunnel transitions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 高差異常需先查基點，不能立刻推定路基局部下沉。","textEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. An unusual level difference requires a datum check before inferring local earthwork settlement.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉陷差與軌道坡折」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Differential settlement and track kink\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。","排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact.","A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b307-v16-29","title":"集水與排水容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「集水與排水容量」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。鐵路集水範圍若只算軌道面，會漏掉坡面與站區流入。 合理化流量法假定雨強與集流條件相符，面積及逕流係數也須明確。它估算峰值流率而非完整洪水歷線；抽水或蓄水設計還需對時間積分和出口條件。 將洞口雨水與隧道滲水分為兩個入流來源。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水與排水容量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. Actual drainage also depends on inlet blockage, pipe slope and downstream water level. Counting only track surface can omit inflow from adjacent slopes and station areas. The rational estimate assumes rainfall intensity compatible with catchment response and explicit area and runoff coefficient. It gives a peak rate, not a complete hydrograph. Pumping or storage design additionally requires time integration and outlet conditions. Separate portal runoff and tunnel seepage into two inflow sources. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.12e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.32436 m^3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.12e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.32436 m^3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「集水與排水容量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-29-k1","title":"集水與排水容量","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity","text":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。鐵路集水範圍若只算軌道面，會漏掉坡面與站區流入。","textEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. Actual drainage also depends on inlet blockage, pipe slope and downstream water level.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集水與排水容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" is correct?","options":["排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位","只要靜態接觸線高度正確就能保證高速受流品質","短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.","Correct static contact-wire height alone guarantees good current collection at high speed.","A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient."],"answer":2,"explanation":"短時逕流可先以降雨強度、集水面積和逕流係數估計，但設施排水還受入口阻塞、管線坡度與下游水位影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A first runoff estimate combines rainfall intensity, catchment area and runoff coefficient. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b307-v16-30","title":"集水與排水容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集水與排水容量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.12e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.32436 m^3/s。敏感度：rain 單獨增加百分之十至 2.332e-05 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.356796 m^3/s。模型邊界：均勻降雨的合理化法概念；不含集流時間、水文頻率分析或蓄滯。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.12e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.32436 m^3/s. Sensitivity: rain, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2.332e-05 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.356796 m^3/s. Model boundary: Uniform-rainfall rational-method concept; concentration time, frequency analysis and storage are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.12e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.32436 m^3/s。敏感度：rain 單獨增加百分之十至 2.332e-05 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 0.356796 m^3/s。模型邊界：均勻降雨的合理化法概念；不含集流時間、水文頻率分析或蓄滯。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.12e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.32436 m^3/s. Sensitivity: rain, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2.332e-05 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.356796 m^3/s. Model boundary: Uniform-rainfall rational-method concept; concentration time, frequency analysis and storage are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集水與排水容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.12e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口","列車截面乘速度就是所有風井各自收到的相同流量"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.","Train frontal area times speed is the identical flow received by every ventilation shaft."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.12e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2；計算：flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.32436 m^3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: coefficient=0.85 1; rain=2.12e-05 m/s; area=18000 m^2; calculation: flow=coefficient*rain*area=0.32436 m^3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b307-v16-31","title":"集水與排水容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集水與排水容量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 核對雨量單位和有效集水邊界，量測泵浦出流與集水井水位變化，以體積守恆互證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verify rainfall units and catchment boundaries, measure pump outflow and sump-level change, and cross-check them through volume conservation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將部分入口視為堵塞，建立地表暫存與排出的水量表；比較增加入口和增加泵量對不同瓶頸的效果。 再以本單元 rain 的對照值重算 flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Block selected inlets in the scenario, tabulate surface storage and discharge, and compare additional inlets with additional pumping for different bottlenecks. Also recalculate flow for the alternative rain value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 核對雨量單位和有效集水邊界，量測泵浦出流與集水井水位變化，以體積守恆互證。","textEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verify rainfall units and catchment boundaries, measure pump outflow and sump-level change, and cross-check them through volume conservation.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將部分入口視為堵塞，建立地表暫存與排出的水量表；比較增加入口和增加泵量對不同瓶頸的效果。 再以本單元 rain 的對照值重算 flow，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Block selected inlets in the scenario, tabulate surface storage and discharge, and compare additional inlets with additional pumping for different bottlenecks. Also recalculate flow for the alternative rain value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集水與排水容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"現地核對集水分界和入口標高，以雨量、液位與泵浦運轉紀錄檢查水量收支，分開分析正常排放和下游頂托。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check catchment boundaries and inlet elevations, use rainfall, water-level and pump logs for a balance, and distinguish normal outflow from downstream backwater. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b307-v16-32","title":"集水與排水容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集水與排水容量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Catchment inflow and drainage capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 排水堵塞改變有效出流，不能只用較大泵浦銘牌值補償。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Blocked drainage changes effective outflow and cannot be compensated merely by a larger pump nameplate rating. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：將洞口雨水與隧道滲水分為兩個入流來源。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Separate portal runoff and tunnel seepage into two inflow sources.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排水管截面夠大就不需要檢查入口堵塞及下游水位」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently large drain eliminates the need to check blocked inlets and tailwater.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 排水堵塞改變有效出流，不能只用較大泵浦銘牌值補償。","textEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Blocked drainage changes effective outflow and cannot be compensated merely by a larger pump nameplate rating.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集水與排水容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Catchment inflow and drainage capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要靜態接觸線高度正確就能保證高速受流品質","垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Correct static contact-wire height alone guarantees good current collection at high speed.","Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause."],"answer":2,"explanation":"垃圾堵塞入口會讓理論管徑容量無法發揮；下游水位上升又可能使出口排量下降，僅加大泵浦不能解決所有原因。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked inlets can prevent nominal pipe capacity from being used, while rising tailwater reduces outflow; a larger pump does not resolve every cause. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b307-v16-s5","title":"接觸線張力波速與煞車熱量與溫升","titleEn":"Contact-wire tension wave speed & Brake heat and temperature rise","description":"本階段聚焦「接觸線張力波速」與「煞車熱量與溫升」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Contact-wire tension wave speed\" and \"Brake heat and temperature rise\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b307-v16-33","title":"接觸線張力波速：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Contact-wire tension wave speed: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「接觸線張力波速」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Contact-wire tension wave speed” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"受電弓擾動會沿接觸線傳播，張力提高使橫波速度上升而線密度增加使波速下降。波速與列車速度的比值提供動態風險線索，但多跨懸掛、吊弦和接觸非線性不能由單根弦模型取代。 線密度決定單位長度的慣性，張力提供恢復作用，因此波速平方與張力成正比。提高張力也改變支承受力；波速裕度只能作篩檢，不能推定接觸力必然均勻。 比較露天和隧道內支承條件改變時的架線動態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接觸線張力波速」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pantograph disturbances propagate along the contact wire. Greater tension raises transverse wave speed, whereas greater mass per length lowers it. The ratio to train speed offers a dynamic clue, but multispan suspension, droppers and contact nonlinearity cannot be replaced by a single-string model. Linear density represents inertia per unit length and tension supplies restoring force, so squared wave speed scales with tension. Higher tension also changes support loading. A wave-speed margin is a screening measure, not proof of uniform contact force. Compare contact-line dynamics when support conditions change between open track and tunnel. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Contact-wire tension wave speed” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：tension=21200 N; density=1.1 kg/m；計算：wave_speed=(tension/density)**0.5=138.8262 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: tension=21200 N; density=1.1 kg/m; calculation: wave_speed=(tension/density)**0.5=138.8262 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要靜態接觸線高度正確就能保證高速受流品質」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Correct static contact-wire height alone guarantees good current collection at high speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接觸線張力波速」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Contact-wire tension wave speed”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-33-k1","title":"接觸線張力波速","titleEn":"Contact-wire tension wave speed","text":"受電弓擾動會沿接觸線傳播，張力提高使橫波速度上升而線密度增加使波速下降。波速與列車速度的比值提供動態風險線索，但多跨懸掛、吊弦和接觸非線性不能由單根弦模型取代。","textEn":"Pantograph disturbances propagate along the contact wire. Greater tension raises transverse wave speed, whereas greater mass per length lowers it.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要靜態接觸線高度正確就能保證高速受流品質 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Correct static contact-wire height alone guarantees good current collection at high speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸線張力波速」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Contact-wire tension wave speed\" is correct?","options":["受電弓擾動會沿接觸線傳播，張力提高使橫波速度上升而線密度增加使波速下降。","只要靜態接觸線高度正確就能保證高速受流品質","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["Pantograph disturbances propagate along the contact wire.","Correct static contact-wire height alone guarantees good current collection at high speed.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"受電弓擾動會沿接觸線傳播，張力提高使橫波速度上升而線密度增加使波速下降。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pantograph disturbances propagate along the contact wire. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b307-v16-34","title":"接觸線張力波速：定量估算","titleEn":"Contact-wire tension wave speed: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接觸線張力波速」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Contact-wire tension wave speed” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：tension=21200 N; density=1.1 kg/m；計算：wave_speed=(tension/density)**0.5=138.8262 m/s。敏感度：tension 單獨增加百分之十至 23320 N，其餘固定，結果為 145.6022 m/s。模型邊界：無彎曲剛度的均勻張弦；不是受流合格判定或允許車速。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: tension=21200 N; density=1.1 kg/m; calculation: wave_speed=(tension/density)**0.5=138.8262 m/s. Sensitivity: tension, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 23320 N, with all other inputs fixed, gives 145.6022 m/s. Model boundary: Uniform tensioned string without bending stiffness; not a current-collection acceptance rule or permitted train speed. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對補償裝置行程、線溫與張力紀錄，再量測受電弓接觸力統計及離線事件，辨別平均值正常但峰值異常。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check compensation travel, wire temperature and tension, then examine contact-force statistics and loss-of-contact events to distinguish acceptable means from abnormal peaks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：tension=21200 N; density=1.1 kg/m；計算：wave_speed=(tension/density)**0.5=138.8262 m/s。敏感度：tension 單獨增加百分之十至 23320 N，其餘固定，結果為 145.6022 m/s。模型邊界：無彎曲剛度的均勻張弦；不是受流合格判定或允許車速。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: tension=21200 N; density=1.1 kg/m; calculation: wave_speed=(tension/density)**0.5=138.8262 m/s. Sensitivity: tension, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 23320 N, with all other inputs fixed, gives 145.6022 m/s. Model boundary: Uniform tensioned string without bending stiffness; not a current-collection acceptance rule or permitted train speed.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接觸線張力波速」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Contact-wire tension wave speed\", which statement holds?","options":["空氣體積流率相同就表示任何海拔的散熱質量流率相同","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：tension=21200 N; density=1.1 kg/m。","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Equal volumetric airflow guarantees equal cooling mass flow at every altitude.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：tension=21200 N; density=1.1 kg/m；計算：wave_speed=(tension/density)**0.5=138.8262 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: tension=21200 N; density=1.1 kg/m; calculation: wave_speed=(tension/density)**0.5=138.8262 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b307-v16-35","title":"接觸線張力波速：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Contact-wire tension wave speed: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接觸線張力波速」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Contact-wire tension wave speed” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對補償裝置行程、線溫與張力紀錄，再量測受電弓接觸力統計及離線事件，辨別平均值正常但峰值異常。 核對接觸線張力、單位長度質量及量測位置，並用接觸力和離線事件檢查動態品質。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check compensation travel, wire temperature and tension, then examine contact-force statistics and loss-of-contact events to distinguish acceptable means from abnormal peaks. Verify contact-wire tension, mass per unit length and measurement location, then examine contact force and loss-of-contact events for dynamic quality. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將張力降低一成和線密度增加一成分別計算波速，列出尚需哪些接觸力量測才能討論動態受流品質。 再以本單元 tension 的對照值重算 wave_speed，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce tension and increase wire mass density separately by ten percent, calculate wave speed, and identify the contact-force measurements still needed to assess dynamic collection. Also recalculate wave_speed for the alternative tension value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：補償裝置卡滯會讓溫度變化改變張力，吊弦鬆弛又會改變局部動態剛度；只讀取靜態高度難以辨識。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A sticking tensioning device lets temperature change tension, while slack droppers change local dynamic stiffness; static wire height alone cannot identify either mechanism. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對補償裝置行程、線溫與張力紀錄，再量測受電弓接觸力統計及離線事件，辨別平均值正常但峰值異常。 核對接觸線張力、單位長度質量及量測位置，並用接觸力和離線事件檢查動態品質。","textEn":"Check compensation travel, wire temperature and tension, then examine contact-force statistics and loss-of-contact events to distinguish acceptable means from abnormal peaks. Verify contact-wire tension, mass per unit length and measurement location, then examine contact force and loss-of-contact events for dynamic quality.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將張力降低一成和線密度增加一成分別計算波速，列出尚需哪些接觸力量測才能討論動態受流品質。 再以本單元 tension 的對照值重算 wave_speed，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Reduce tension and increase wire mass density separately by ten percent, calculate wave speed, and identify the contact-force measurements still needed to assess dynamic collection. Also recalculate wave_speed for the alternative tension value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接觸線張力波速」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Contact-wire tension wave speed\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","橋梁跨長增加一成其彈性撓度最多只增加一成","核對補償裝置行程、線溫與張力紀錄，再量測受電弓接觸力統計及離線事件，辨別平均值正常但峰值異常。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Increasing bridge span by ten percent increases elastic deflection by at most ten percent.","Check compensation travel, wire temperature and tension, then examine contact-force statistics and loss-of-contact events to distinguish acceptable means from abnormal peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對補償裝置行程、線溫與張力紀錄，再量測受電弓接觸力統計及離線事件，辨別平均值正常但峰值異常。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check compensation travel, wire temperature and tension, then examine contact-force statistics and loss-of-contact events to distinguish acceptable means from abnormal peaks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b307-v16-36","title":"接觸線張力波速：失效診斷","titleEn":"Contact-wire tension wave speed: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接觸線張力波速」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Contact-wire tension wave speed” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"補償裝置卡滯會讓溫度變化改變張力，吊弦鬆弛又會改變局部動態剛度；只讀取靜態高度難以辨識。 波速符合估算仍可能離線，需查看接觸力的時間歷程。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A sticking tensioning device lets temperature change tension, while slack droppers change local dynamic stiffness; static wire height alone cannot identify either mechanism. Agreement in wave-speed estimates does not rule out contact loss; inspect contact-force histories. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較露天和隧道內支承條件改變時的架線動態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare contact-line dynamics when support conditions change between open track and tunnel.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要靜態接觸線高度正確就能保證高速受流品質」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Correct static contact-wire height alone guarantees good current collection at high speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"補償裝置卡滯會讓溫度變化改變張力，吊弦鬆弛又會改變局部動態剛度；只讀取靜態高度難以辨識。 波速符合估算仍可能離線，需查看接觸力的時間歷程。","textEn":"A sticking tensioning device lets temperature change tension, while slack droppers change local dynamic stiffness; static wire height alone cannot identify either mechanism. Agreement in wave-speed estimates does not rule out contact loss; inspect contact-force histories.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接觸線張力波速」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Contact-wire tension wave speed\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補償裝置卡滯會讓溫度變化改變張力，吊弦鬆弛又會改變局部動態剛度；只讀取靜態高度難以辨識。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點"],"optionsEn":["A sticking tensioning device lets temperature change tension, while slack droppers change local dynamic stiffness.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots."],"answer":0,"explanation":"補償裝置卡滯會讓溫度變化改變張力，吊弦鬆弛又會改變局部動態剛度；只讀取靜態高度難以辨識。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A sticking tensioning device lets temperature change tension, while slack droppers change local dynamic stiffness; static wire height alone cannot identify either mechanism. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b307-v16-37","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「煞車熱量與溫升」如何影響山陽新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Brake heat and temperature rise” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sanyo Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。短時平均模型無法描述表面熱點、對流冷卻或熱裂紋，需要把能量分配與熱擴散分開。 有效受熱質量可以小於構件總質量，短時接觸表面的熱量也未必已傳到內部。能量平衡應先界定摩擦分配比例，再評估對流、輻射和間歇冷卻是否可忽略。 在連續減速情境下區分單次熱量與尚未散去的殘熱。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「煞車熱量與溫升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths. Average temperature rise is allocated energy divided by thermal capacity. A short-duration lumped model cannot describe surface hot spots, cooling or thermal cracks; energy allocation and thermal diffusion are separate questions. The effective heated mass can be smaller than total component mass, and short-duration surface heat may not reach the interior. First define frictional energy allocation, then assess whether convection, radiation and cooling between events can be neglected. Distinguish one braking event’s heat from residual heat during repeated deceleration. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Brake heat and temperature rise” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.272e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=125.6917 K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.272e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=125.6917 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「煞車熱量與溫升」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Brake heat and temperature rise”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-37-k1","title":"煞車熱量與溫升","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise","text":"未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。短時平均模型無法描述表面熱點、對流冷卻或熱裂紋，需要把能量分配與熱擴散分開。","textEn":"Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths. Average temperature rise is allocated energy divided by thermal capacity.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「煞車熱量與溫升」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Brake heat and temperature rise\" is correct?","options":["煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點","未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.","Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":1,"explanation":"未回收的動能會在摩擦煞車與阻力路徑中轉成熱，平均溫升由分配到構件的能量除以熱容量決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Unrecovered kinetic energy becomes heat through friction brakes and resistance paths. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b307-v16-38","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：定量估算","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「煞車熱量與溫升」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Brake heat and temperature rise” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.272e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=125.6917 K。敏感度：energy 單獨增加百分之十至 1.3992e+07 J，其餘固定，結果為 138.2609 K。模型邊界：均勻溫度且無散熱、常數比熱；不推定摩擦材極限。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.272e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=125.6917 K. Sensitivity: energy, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1.3992e+07 J, with all other inputs fixed, gives 138.2609 K. Model boundary: Uniform temperature without heat loss and with constant heat capacity; no friction-material limit is inferred. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.272e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=125.6917 K。敏感度：energy 單獨增加百分之十至 1.3992e+07 J，其餘固定，結果為 138.2609 K。模型邊界：均勻溫度且無散熱、常數比熱；不推定摩擦材極限。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.272e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=125.6917 K. Sensitivity: energy, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 1.3992e+07 J, with all other inputs fixed, gives 138.2609 K. Model boundary: Uniform temperature without heat loss and with constant heat capacity; no friction-material limit is inferred.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「煞車熱量與溫升」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Brake heat and temperature rise\", which statement holds?","options":["列車截面乘速度就是所有風井各自收到的相同流量","任何速度下增加超高都一定減少車內橫向加速度","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.272e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)。"],"optionsEn":["Train frontal area times speed is the identical flow received by every ventilation shaft.","Increasing cant always reduces lateral acceleration at every operating speed.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：energy=1.272e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K)；計算：rise=energy/(mass*cp)=125.6917 K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: energy=1.272e+07 J; mass=220 kg; cp=460 J/(kg*K); calculation: rise=energy/(mass*cp)=125.6917 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b307-v16-39","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「煞車熱量與溫升」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Brake heat and temperature rise” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。 在不同深度保留溫度曲線並核對感測器反應時間，用初末能量平衡檢查平均溫升。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity. Retain temperature histories at different depths, verify sensor response time, and use initial-to-final energy balance to check mean temperature rise. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將同一能量分給兩種有效熱容量，計算平均溫升後設計能辨認熱點的量測網格，說明集中參數模型缺少哪些資訊。 再以本單元 energy 的對照值重算 rise，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Allocate equal energy to two effective thermal capacities, calculate average rise, and design a measurement grid for hot spots while identifying information missing from the lumped model. Also recalculate rise for the alternative energy value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。 在不同深度保留溫度曲線並核對感測器反應時間，用初末能量平衡檢查平均溫升。","textEn":"Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity. Retain temperature histories at different depths, verify sensor response time, and use initial-to-final energy balance to check mean temperature rise.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將同一能量分給兩種有效熱容量，計算平均溫升後設計能辨認熱點的量測網格，說明集中參數模型缺少哪些資訊。 再以本單元 energy 的對照值重算 rise，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Allocate equal energy to two effective thermal capacities, calculate average rise, and design a measurement grid for hot spots while identifying information missing from the lumped model. Also recalculate rise for the alternative energy value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「煞車熱量與溫升」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Brake heat and temperature rise\"?","options":["以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以熱電偶與紅外量測交叉檢查溫升，記錄煞車能量、環境溫度與冷卻時間，並校正紅外放射率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-check temperature rise with thermocouples and infrared measurements, record braking energy, ambient temperature and cooling time, and calibrate infrared emissivity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b307-v16-40","title":"煞車熱量與溫升：失效診斷","titleEn":"Brake heat and temperature rise: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"prerequisiteIds":["b307-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「煞車熱量與溫升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Brake heat and temperature rise” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 若表面與內部溫差很大，集中熱容量假設便不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. A large surface-to-core temperature difference indicates that the lumped thermal-capacity assumption is insufficient. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在連續減速情境下區分單次熱量與尚未散去的殘熱。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Distinguish one braking event’s heat from residual heat during repeated deceleration.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「煞車盤平均溫度低就能保證局部沒有熱點」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low mean brake-disc temperature guarantees the absence of local hot spots.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b307-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 若表面與內部溫差很大，集中熱容量假設便不足。","textEn":"Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. A large surface-to-core temperature difference indicates that the lumped thermal-capacity assumption is insufficient.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]},{"id":"b307-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「煞車熱量與溫升」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Brake heat and temperature rise\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部接觸不均會產生熱點，即使平均溫升不高仍可能形成熱裂紋；錯誤放射率也會掩蓋真實表面溫度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uneven contact can create hot spots and thermal cracks despite a modest mean rise; incorrect emissivity can also conceal the actual surface temperature. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-b307-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b307-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b307-en.svg"}};
